1 Introduction
The Data Integration and Visualization Software is a web-based application designed to manage projects, administrative records, and generate interactive data visualizations from uploaded datasets. The system allows authorized users to organize files, track project-related activities, upload structured data, and create analytical plots for comparative analysis.
This manual provides step-by-step guidance for using the system, including login, project management, record handling, data upload, visualization, and system settings.
2 User Roles and Access Levels
Access to system features depends on the assigned user role.
Admin
•	Create and manage users
•	Assign roles and permissions
•	View dashboard statistics
•	Manage projects
•	Access all modules
User
•	Access assigned projects
•	Upload and manage datasets
•	Generate visualizations
•	Manage records within allowed modules
2.1 Login Procedure
•	Open the application.
•	Enter your registered email address.
•	Enter your password.
•	Click Login.
If login fails, verify credentials or contact the administrator.
 
Figure 1: Login Page
3 Admin Dashboard 
After successful login, the system opens the Dashboard page. The dashboard provides an overview of system users and allows administrators to create new users.
The User Overview panel displays a summary of all registered users in the system.
The panel includes:
•	Total number of users
•	Role-wise distribution of users:
•	Group Directors
•	Team Leads
•	System Managers
•	Junior Research Fellows
•	Contract Engineers
Each role displays the total count along with a visual icon for quick identification. This section helps administrators monitor user distribution across different roles.
3.1 User Creation 
The “Create New User” section allows administrators to add new users to the system.
To create a new user:
•	Enter the User Name.
•	Select the appropriate Role from the dropdown list.
•	Enter the Login ID (email address).
•	Enter the Password.
•	Click the Create button.
The system performs validation to ensure all required fields are completed. A confirmation message is displayed upon successful user creation. The password field includes a visibility toggle to allow users to view or hide the entered password.
             
Figure 2: Admin Dashboard Page
3.2 User Management :
The User Management page allows administrators to view, search, and manage all registered users in the system.
 
Figure 3: User Management Page
Manage User Login
This section displays a tabular list of all users with the following details:
•	Name – Registered user name
•	Role – Assigned role (e.g., TL, SM, GD, ADMIN)
•	Email – User login ID
•	Access – Access level identifier
•	Active Status – Indicates whether the user account is active
•	Created Date – Date and time of user creation
•	Last Login – Most recent login timestamp
Search Functionality
The search bar allows administrators to search users by:
•	Name
•	Email
•	Role
This enables quick filtering of user records
User Actions
The Actions column provides administrative controls:
•	Change Password – Reset or update the user's password
•	Delete User – Remove a user from the system
3.3 Reset User Password 
         The Admin user can reset or change the password of any registered user through the User Management section. In the Manage User Login page, the administrator can view the list of users and their details. To change a password, click the Change Password icon in the Actions column for the selected user. A Change Password dialog box will appear where the administrator can enter a new password and click Save to update it or Cancel to discard the changes.
 
Figure 4: Change Password Dialog Page
4 Management Dashboard Overview:
The Manager Dashboard Overview page provides a summary of project statistics and quick access to project management features.
4.1 Dashboard Components
4.1.1 Summary 
At the top of the dashboard, statistical summary cards display:
•	Total Projects
•	CFD Data Count
•	Wind Data Count
•	Flight Data Count
•	Aero Data Count
•	Total Reports
These cards provide a quick overview of system activity and uploaded dataset volumes.
Projects Section
The Projects panel displays all available projects in a structured list format.
Each project entry includes:
•	Project Name
•	Status (Active/Inactive)
•	Short Description
•	Created Date
•	Member Count
•	View Project Button
Clicking the View Project button navigates to the selected project’s detailed page.
Data Distribution and Reports Panel
The right-side panel displays:
•	Data Distribution Overview
•	Reports Summary
If no data is available, a placeholder message is shown. Once datasets and reports are added, the panels update automatically.
 
Figure 5: Dashboard Overview Page
To open a project, click the View Project button corresponding to the desired project. After clicking View Project, the system navigates to the Project Overview page. This page provides access to the project workspace where users can manage datasets and navigate to different modules
 
Figure 6: Project Overview Page
4.1.2 Create New Project
 
	Figure 7: Add Project Page
To create a new project:
•	Click the + New Project button.
•	Enter the Project Name.
•	Provide a Project Description.
•	Add Members (search by name or email).
•	Click Create.
The newly created project will appear in the Projects list.
4.1.3 Notification Panel
 
Figure 8: Notification Panel Page
The Notification Panel allows users to receive updates about important activities performed within the project, such as completion of visualization processing or other system events. The notification icon is located at the top-right corner of the application header. When a new event occurs, the icon displays a notification count badge indicating the number of unread notifications.
By clicking on the notification icon, users can view a list of recent notifications along with the corresponding message and timestamp. Notifications inform users about events such as visualization completion, system updates, or other processing results. Users can also mark all notifications as read by selecting the “Mark all as read” option available in the notification panel.
4.2 Minutes of Meeting
The Minutes of Meeting module allows users to upload, manage, and track meeting minutes along with associated action items. Meetings can be organized under different meeting categories and linked to specific projects where applicable.
 
	Figure 9: Minutes of meeting Page
4.2.1 Meeting Categories
Users can switch between different meeting types using the tabs:
•	Technology Council (TCM)
•	PMRC
•	Executive Board Meeting
•	Group Director Meeting
For PMRC and Executive Board meetings, users have the option to associate the meeting minutes with a specific project.
4.2.2 Upload Meeting Minutes
 
Figure 10: Upload Meeting Minutes Page
To upload a new meeting record:
•	Click Upload Minutes.
•	Browse and select a PDF or Word file.
•	Enter Action Points.
•	Assign action owners (optional).
•	Select the Meeting Date.
•	Enter a Tag Name.
•	Click Upload MOM.
Supported formats include PDF and Word documents.

Managing Action Points
Each meeting can contain multiple action points assigned to users.
Users can:
•	Add new action points
•	Assign responsibilities to individuals or teams
•	Edit existing actions
•	Mark actions as completed
4.2.3 My Action – View and Edit
The “My Action” window allows users to view or modify assigned action points.
The page displays:
•	Tag Name
•	Meeting Date
•	Assigned Person
•	Action Description
•	Completion Status
Users can switch between:
•	View Action – Displays action details
•	Edit Action – Modify action description or assignment
Actions can be marked as completed when tasks are finished.
 
Figure 11: View Action Page
 
Figure 12: Edit Action Page
4.2.4 Task Assignment and Notification
When action points are assigned to users while creating or editing a meeting record, the system automatically sends a task notification to the assigned users.
 
Figure 13: Task Assigned Notification 
The notification appears in the notification panel (bell icon) located at the top-right corner of the application.
The notification contains:
•	Meeting category 
•	Meeting title or tag name
•	Meeting date
•	Assigned action description
This alert informs the assigned user that a new task has been created and requires attention.
Users can open the notification and click Okay to acknowledge the assigned task.
4.2.5 Task Acknowledgement
After receiving the task notification, the assigned user can acknowledge the task by confirming the notification.
 
Figure 14: Task Acknowledged Notification 
When the user clicks Okay, the system records the acknowledgement and sends a confirmation notification to the meeting creator.
The acknowledgement message informs the creator that the assigned user has reviewed and accepted the task.
4.3 Student Engagement
The Student Engagement module allows users to manage student internship and academic programs. It provides functionality to add, edit, view, filter, and delete student program records while tracking program progress and associated documentation.
 
Figure 15: Student Engagement Dashboard Page
4.3.1 Dashboard Overview
The top section displays summary cards such as:
•	Total Students
•	Internships
•	Ongoing Programs
•	Completed Programs
These cards provide a quick overview of student engagement statistics.
Users can also:
•	Filter records by Type
•	Filter records by Status
Add new student program using the Add Student button
Student Programs Table
The Student Programs table displays all registered student records with the following details:
•	Student Name
•	College Name
•	Project Title
•	Program Type
•	Duration
•	Start Date
•	End Date
•	Guide / Mentor
•	Status (Ongoing / Completed)
•	Actions (View, Edit, Delete)
Users can perform the following actions:
•	View program details
•	Edit existing program information
•	Delete a program record
4.3.2 Upload Student Program
To add a new student program:
•	Click Add Student.
•	Upload supporting document (PDF/Word format).
•	Enter Student Name.
•	Enter College Name.
•	Enter Project Title.
•	Select Program Type (e.g., Internship).
•	Select Start Date and End Date.
•	Enter Program Duration (in months).
•	Enter Guide Name.
•	Select Program Status (Ongoing / Completed).
•	Click Add Program to save.
 
Figure 16: Student Program Modal Page
