These summary indicators provide a quick overview of procurement activity.
 
Figure 17: Procurement Record Dashboard Page
Supply Order Table
The Supply Order table displays all procurement entries with the following details:
•	ID
•	Particulars
•	Budget Name
•	Quantity (QTY)
•	Duration
•	Start Date
•	Delivery Date
•	BO Order Number
•	Purchase Order Number
•	Amount
•	Status
•	Actions
Users can search records using the search bar and apply filters based on type or status.

Status Tracking
Each procurement record displays its current status:
•	Ongoing
•	Completed
Status can be updated when delivery is completed or procurement is finalized.
Available Actions
In the Actions column, users can:
•	View details
•	Edit procurement record
•	Delete record
4.4.2 Upload Supply Order
        
Figure 18: Add Supply Order Page
1. To create a new procurement record:
2. Click the Procurement Record button.
3. Upload a supporting document (if required).
4. Enter the following details:
•	BO Number
•	Particulars
•	Supply Name
•	Quantity
•	Delivery Date
•	Start Date
•	BO Order
•	Purchase Order Number
•	Status
•	Quantity Allocation
•	Amount
5. Click Submit Record to save.
4.4.3 Assigning Quantities
The system allows splitting the total quantity among different individuals, teams, or locations.
To assign quantities:
1. Click Manage Assignees.
2. Enter:
•	Number of Items
•	Assign To (Name or Location)
3. Click Add Assignee.
4. Review:
•	Total Quantity
•	Assigned Quantity
•	Remaining Quantity
5. Click Done to confirm.
The system automatically calculates remaining quantity and prevents over-allocation.
 
Figure 19: Assignees Allocation Page
4.5 Budget Estimation
The Budget Estimation module allows users to create, manage, and track forecast budget records for different financial years. Users can upload supporting documents, enter financial details, and categorize expenses based on project requirements.

Figure 20: Budget Estimation Dashboard Page
4.5.1 Budget Overview
The top section of the page includes:
•	Search bar 
•	Financial Year selector 
•	Type filter
•	Additional filter options
•	Upload Forecast Budget button
These controls allow users to filter and manage budget records efficiently.
Forecast Budget Table
The Forecast Budget table displays all recorded budget entries with details such as:
•	Cash Outgo Split Year
•	TDCC Feasibility
•	Reusability for Other Projects
•	Necessity of Hardware Technologies
•	Initiation of Condemnation of Store
•	Capital or Revenue Classification
•	Notes
•	Attachment
•	Action options
Users can:
•	View attachment
•	Edit budget record
•	Download document
•	Delete record

Document Attachment
Each budget record can include a document attachment for reference. Users can:
•	View attached file
•	Download file
•	Replace file during edit
•	Supported formats: PDF and Word.
Editing and Deleting Records
Users can:
•	Edit financial details
•	Modify classification fields
•	Update notes
•	Delete records if no longer required
4.5.2 Upload Forecast Budget
To add a new forecast budget:
1.	Click Upload Forecast Budget.
2.	Upload supporting document (PDF/Word format).
3.	Select Forecast Year.
4.	Enter Division Name.
5.	Enter Item details.
6.	Enter Quantity (QTY).
7.	Enter Existing Stock.
8.	Enter Estimated Cost.
9.	Enter Demand Indication Months.
10.	Select Capital or Revenue.
11.	Enter Project or Build details.
12.	Enter DPP 2020 Serial Number.
13.	Enter Likely Cash Outgo amount.
14.	Select TDCC feasibility.
15.	Select Reusability for other projects.
16.	Select necessity of hardware technologies.
17.	Select initiation of condemnation of store.
18.	Add Notes (if required).
19.	Click Upload to save.
 
Figure 21: Upload Forecast Budget Page
