This section helps users understand the purpose and scope of the system.
Version Information
The version section displays the current application version (e.g., Version 2025.0).
This helps in:
Tracking system updates
•	Identifying build versions
•	Supporting maintenance and troubleshooting
5 Project Overview
At the top of the page, basic project information is displayed:
•	Project Name
•	Project Status (e.g., Active)
•	Project Description
•	Created Date
•	Member Count
 
Figure 33: Project Overview Page
5.1 Dataset Tabs
Project data is categorized into four dataset types:
•	CFD Data
•	Wind Tunnel Data
•	Flight Data
•	Others
Key behavior:
•	Only one dataset tab can be active at a time.
•	Switching between dataset tabs refreshes the displayed tags and file list.
•	Each dataset maintains its own independent set of tags and associated files.
This ensures structured organization of project data by category.
Tag / Folder Management
Within each dataset, files are organized under Tags or Folders.
The table displays:
•	Tag / Folder Name
•	Processing Status (if applicable)
•	Created Date
•	Action options (Edit, Delete)
•	Go To navigation button
Users can:
•	Rename a tag
•	Delete a tag
•	Navigate to tag-specific data

This section provides a quick summary of the selected project.
5.2 Edit Project
Users can edit project details using the Edit option.
The Edit Project modal allows:
•	Viewing the Project Name (cannot be changed after creation).
•	Updating the Project Description.
•	Adding new members using name or email search.
•	Removing existing members.
•	Saving changes or cancelling the update.
The project name remains fixed to maintain data integrity.
 
Figure 34: Project Edit Page
5.3 Project Members
The Project Members view displays:
•	Member Name
•	Member Email ID
This provides a clear list of all users assigned to the project.
 
Figure 35: Project Members Page




5.4 Upload File

 
Figure 36: Upload Files Page

Clicking the Upload File button opens the upload modal.
The upload modal allows users to:
•	Browse and select plot files.
•	Preview selected files (if supported).
•	Enter Folder / Tag Name.
•	Select Data Type (e.g., CFD).
•	Upload selected files.
Upload Modal Modes
The upload modal operates in two modes:
Create Mode
•	Upload files under a new tag.
•	A new folder is created for the selected dataset.

Edit Mode
•	Rename an existing tag.
•	Upload additional files to an existing tag.
File Processing and Navigation
After upload:
•	Files are associated with the selected dataset and tag.
•	Users can navigate to the dataset view using the “Go To” action button.
•	Processing status indicators (if applicable) are displayed next to tags.
File Selection
Select Files
•	The user clicks Browse Plot Files to select one or more files.
•	Multiple files can be selected at once.
Supported File Types
File behavior depends on the format:
1.	CSV / Excel / TXT / DAT / C files
•	Eligible for preview.
•	Can be used for visualization.
2.	Images and other file formats
•	Stored as raw files only.
After selection, the system displays:
•	File Name
•	File Type
•	File Size
•	Visualization eligibility (enabled only for supported tabular files)
Provide tag and data type
•	the user enters a Folder / Tag Name, which groups the uploaded files.
•	The user selects a Data Type (CFD, Wind Data, Flight Data. Others). In edit mode, the data type is fixed and cannot be changed.
5.5 Configure Plot File Headers 
Once tabular file is selected, the Plot File Header option appears.
Users can choose how headers are handled:
•	Use headers from file – system reads the first row
•	File has no headers – system auto-generates column names.
•	Provide custom headers – user manually enters comma-separated headers.
•	When custom headers are used: users can manually define custom headers, which can be applied to one or multiple selected files using the “Apply custom headers to all files” option
 
Figure 37: Upload Files Page
5.6 Select file for preview
	Clicking a file from the list loads it into the Preview panel.
	The preview adapts automatically based on file type.
Image files: a visual preview of the image is displayed.
 
Figure 38: Image Files Upload and preview Page

Excel files: all available sheets are listed. Users can switch between sheets and select which sheets should be included for visualization.
 
Figure 39: Upload and preview of Excel Files
 Dat / .c text files:
1.	The preview displays the line-by-line with line numbers.
2.	Total line count is shown.
3.	The user can select start line and end line.
4.	Only the selected range is parsed, used for data extraction, used for plotting graphs.
5.	Selected range is visually highlighted.
6.	The system auto-detects headers from the first selected line.
7.	The parsed data range is also shown as a table preview.
 
Figure 40: Upload and preview for .Dat Files









•	Apply line range to multiple files
 
Figure 41: Apply range for Files Page
	For .Dat and .c files, users can enable “Apply range to all .Dat /.c files”.
	This applies the same start and end line selection to all similar files, ensuing consistency and reducing manual effort.
MAT (MATLAB) Files:
	The preview displays all variables available in the .mat file along with their dimensions and data types.
	When a variable is selected, its data is shown in a tabular format.
	Users can define a slice range to load only a specific portion of the data.
	After clicking Apply, only the selected slice is displayed and processed.
	The selected data is prepared for further parsing and visualization.
 
                                             Figure 42: MAT file preview

•	Upload and processing
	When user clicks upload.
	A progress bar shows upload status.
	Files are uploaded along with: dataset type, tag name, header configuration, selected sheets, selected line ranges.
	Visualization-enabled files are queued for processing.
	Non- visualized files are stored as raw files.
 
Figure 43: Stored Files Page
5.7 Raw preview page:
The Raw Preview page displays the data exactly as it was uploaded, without any changes.
 
Figure 44: Raw Preview Page
5.8 Processed Preview Page:
The Processed Preview page displays data that has been parsed and prepared for plotting. Users can edit the column headers on this page.
 
Figure 45: Processed Preview Page
5.9 Global Search
The Global Search feature allows users to quickly find different sections, tags, files, and visualizations within a project. The search bar is located at the top-right corner of the Project Overview page.
Users can enter keywords related to project sections or content. As the user types, the system displays matching results such as Project Overview, Visualize, Minutes of the Meeting, Technical Reports, Digital Library, Student Engagement, and other available sections within the project. Selecting a result will automatically navigate the user to the corresponding section.
This feature helps users quickly access specific project components without manually browsing through the navigation menu.
 
Figure 46: Global Search Page
6 Visualization:
The Visualization module enables users to generate interactive analytical plots from processed datasets across CFD, Wind Tunnel, and Flight data domains.
The system supports:
•	Multi-dimensional plotting (2D & 3D)
•	Large dataset visualization
•	Multi-series comparison (Overplot)
•	Logarithmic scaling
•	Derived data visualization
6.1 Visualization Workflow
Dataset
   ↓
Tag / Folder
   ↓
Processed File
   ↓
Column Selection
   ↓
Plot Type Selection
   ↓
Axis Assignment
   ↓
Generate Plot
   ↓
Preview / Save
6.2 Plot Type Classification
A. 2D Plots (Primary Analysis)
•	Line Plot
•	Scatter Plot
•	Bar Chart
•	Histogram
•	Box Plot
•	Violin Plot
Used for trend analysis, comparisons, and distributions.
B. Specialized 2D Plots
•	Polar Plot
•	Contour Plot
•	Heatmap
 Used for aerodynamic and multi-variable analysis.
C. 3D Plots
•	3D Scatter
•	3D Line
•	3D Surface
Used for multi-dimensional visualization.
6.3 Plot Descriptions
Line Plot
Represents trends over continuous variables.
Example: Altitude vs Time (Flight Data)
Scatter Plot
Shows relationship between two variables.
Example: Lift vs Drag
Bar Chart
Compares discrete categories.
Histogram
Shows frequency distribution.

Box / Violin
Displays statistical spread and density.
Contour Plot
Requires X, Y, Z data
Displays value distribution as contour levels
Example: CL vs Mach & Angle of Attack
Polar Plot
Used for angular datasets
Example: Lift coefficient vs Angle of Attack
Heatmap
Displays intensity variation
3D Surface Plot
Represents continuous surface
Example: Pressure distribution over wing surface




